<title>USA: Full list of U.S. Senate election races.</title>
<headline>Full list of U.S. Senate election races.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a full list by state of the 34 U.S. Senate election races on Tuesday. Republicans now hold a 53-47 majority in the 100-seat Senate.</p>
<p>STATE		   REPUBLICAN		 DEMOCRAT</p>
<p>-----		   ----------		 --------</p>
<p>Alabama (OD)	  Jeff Sessions	    Roger Bedford</p>
<p>Alaska (IR)	   Ted Stevens		Teresa Obermeyer</p>
<p>Arkansas (OD)	 Tim Hutchinson	   Winston Bryant</p>
<p>Colorado (OR)	 Wayne Allard	     Tom Strickland</p>
<p>Delaware (ID)	 Ray Clatworthy	   Joe Biden</p>
<p>Georgia (OD)	  Guy Millner		Max Cleland</p>
<p>Idaho (IR)	    Larry Craig		Walt Minnick</p>
<p>Illinois (OD)	 Al Salvi		   Dick Durbin</p>
<p>Iowa (ID)	     Jim Ross Lightfoot     Tom Harkin</p>
<p>Kansas (OR)	   Pat Roberts		Sally Thompson</p>
<p>Kansas (OR)	   Sam Brownback	    Jill Docking</p>
<p>Kentucky (IR)	 Mitch McConnell	  Steve Beshear</p>
<p>Louisiana (OD)	Woody Jenkins	    Mary Landrieu</p>
<p>Maine (OR)	    Susan Collins	    Joe Brennan</p>
<p>Massachusetts (ID)  William Weld	     John Kerry</p>
<p>Michigan (ID)	 Ronna Romney	     Carl Levin</p>
<p>Minnesota (ID)	Rudy Boschwitz	   Paul Wellstone</p>
<p>Mississippi (IR)    Thad Cochran	     James Hunt</p>
<p>Montana (ID)	  Dennis Rehberg	   Max Baucus</p>
<p>Nebraska (OD)	 Chuck Hagel		Ben Nelson</p>
<p>New Hampshire (IR)  Bob Smith		  Dick Swett</p>
<p>New Jersey (OD)     Dick Zimmer		Bob Torricelli</p>
<p>New Mexico (IR)     Pete Domenici	    Art Trujillo</p>
<p>North Carolina (IR) Jesse Helms		Harvey Gantt</p>
<p>Oklahoma (IR)	 Jim Inhofe		 Jim Boren</p>
<p>Oregon (OR)	   Gordon Smith	     Tom Bruggere</p>
<p>Rhode Island (OD)   Nancy Mayer		Jack Reed</p>
<p>South Carolina (IR) Strom Thurmond	   Elliott Close</p>
<p>South Dakota (IR)   Larry Pressler	   Tim Johnson</p>
<p>Tennessee (IR)	Fred Thompson	    Houston Gordon</p>
<p>Texas (IR)	    Phil Gramm		 Victor Morales</p>
<p>Virginia (IR)	 John Warner		Mark Warner</p>
<p>West Virginia (ID)  Betty Burkes	     Jay Rockefeller</p>
<p>Wyoming (OR)	  Mike Enzi		  Kathy Karpan</p>
<p>IR = Incumbent Republican</p>
<p>ID = Incumbent Democrat</p>
<p>OR = Open seat, left by Republican</p>
<p>OD = Open seat, left by Democrat</p>
<p>Total number of Republican incumbents - 13</p>
<p>Total number of Democratic incumbents - 7</p>
<p>    Open seats, left by Republicans	 - 6</p>
<p>    Open seats, left by Democrats	   - 8</p>
<p>							  --</p>
<p>			 Total Senate races	 34</p>
